        "content": "# Characters\n\n## Relational suspicion under cooperation\n- Observation: Su Mu treats cooperation as an exchange of tested value rather than immediate trust; Lin Yuwei's bargaining and his deliberate withholding create a relationship that advances through transactions, teasing, and verified risk.\n- Voice: Su Mu favors short strategic statements, dry internal judgments, and action before explanation; Lin Yuwei answers with direct challenge and defensive humor.\n- Controls: Keep trust changes tied to a concrete exchange, rescue, injury, or revealed cost; do not convert pragmatic cooperation into unearned intimacy.\n- Confidence: 0.91\n- Chapter range: 28-41\n- Subject IDs: su-mu, lin-yuwei\n- Evidence: `book-01-8ca152d8 · segment-0028 · lines 5946-6000`\n\n",
