        "content": "# Plot\n\n## Literary Arc: from isolated survival to negotiated interdependence\n- Observation: The survival loop expands from solo scouting and loot selection into a chain of cooperation, trade, shared danger, and new uncertainty; each gain opens a larger tactical or social problem.\n- Interpretation: Escalation works when a concrete resource or threat forces a choice, the choice produces a visible cost, and the consequence changes the next route or relationship.\n- State before: Su Mu has a protected vehicle and strong tactical advantage but limited social information.\n- State after: He has usable cooperation with selected survivors while the world contains threats and rules that cannot be solved by strength alone.\n- Literary Arc IDs: literary-arc-survival-to-network\n- Confidence: 0.92\n- Chapter range: 1-50\n- Subject IDs: su-mu, lin-yuwei, zhou-zhenguo\n- Evidence: `book-01-8ca152d8 · segment-0039 · lines 7940-8020`\n\n",
